# Raw source data (huge TSVs) — never committed.
data/*

# The combined methylation matrix is ~460 MB, over GitHub's hard 100 MB
# per-file limit. It is the ETL input; the per-chromosome splits
# (portal/data/meth_chr*.parquet, each <50 MB) are what the portal serves
# and what gets committed. Regenerate with portal/split_methylation.py.
portal/data/meth_discovery.parquet

# Local DuckDB catalog — rebuilt by etl.py, not needed by the static site.
portal/data/chordoma.duckdb

# The filename map belongs to the published build only. If it lands in site/,
# local dev requests tokenized names that do not exist on disk (404s, and
# DuckDB-WASM reports them as an opaque WebAssembly error). The deploy
# workflow generates it into the build directory instead.
site/datamap.json
datamap.json

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
